From 02173bd980e16bf8e49bc5809345006ae20f5fd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:31:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades] Reboot comes back to LibreELEC Hades, also where
 Windows comes first

On a PC with Windows and Hades, Windows comes first in the boot order of the UEFI firmware and Hades is started for
one start (from the boot menu of the firmware, or by "Restart into LibreELEC Hades"). "Reboot" then ended in Windows:
so did the restart that an add-on or the settings ask for, the one after which an update is applied, and the one that
a boot option of the settings asks for. The restarts that the system makes itself come back to Hades already
(hades-bootnext again); now Reboot does as well, and "Restart into Windows", just under it, is the way to Windows.

CPowerManager::Reboot, the way of every restart of Kodi (builtins Reboot, Reset and Restart, JSON-RPC, Python, the
boot options), asks /usr/lib/libreelec/hades-bootnext again --keep-chosen before the restart: BootNext = the entry that
this start came from (BootCurrent), which the firmware deletes when it uses it. Nothing is written where a plain
restart starts this system already, where the next start was chosen already in this start (by "Restart into
Windows", whose BootNext is left as it is), where the firmware does not say which entry this start came from, or on a
start by BIOS. It never stops the restart. kodi.log says where the restart goes ("Hades boot: 'Reboot' comes back to
this system: BootNext=0003", "...chosen already...", "...goes by the boot order of the firmware...").

The line of kodi.log about "Restart into Windows" now says that Windows comes first in the boot order, not that a
plain restart starts it.

Tested: the answer of the helper is read by ParseKeepResult (gtest, 7 tests; 8 mutants make them fail); the helper
itself in its host test (keep-chosen with a chosen BootNext, with none, on a start by BIOS, with Hades first).
